# Essence Channeler: "Once Essence Channeler has been blocked by a creature without flying or reach, losing life to give it
# flying and vigilance won't cause it to become unblocked" (ruling 2024-07-26; CR 509.1h, 506.4). Bot1 attacks with the
# Channeler, which has no flying (Bot1 has lost no life), and Bot2's Ornithopter blocks it. In the declare blockers step Bot1
# pays 1 life for Marsh Flats: the Channeler now has flying and vigilance, but it stays blocked and stays tapped (vigilance only
# matters as attackers are declared, CR 702.20b). It deals its 2 damage to the Ornithopter, none to Bot2.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Plains
Essence Channeler
Marsh Flats
Plains x3
Plains x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x6
Island x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Essence Channeler.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Marsh Flats.Play
Bot1.Attack(Essence Channeler)
Bot2.Block(Ornithopter > Essence Channeler)
[T3 Bot1.DeclareBlockers]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Essence Channeler.Keywords = (absent)
Bot1.Battlefield.Marsh Flats.Activate
Bot1.Search(Plains)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 19
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter
Bot1.Battlefield.Essence Channeler.Keywords = Flying; Vigilance
Bot1.Battlefield.Essence Channeler.Tapped = true
